# Denies every request. Seeded by the framework installer (seed-once) into the
# stores that must NEVER be web-reachable: data/, config/, logs/. In the
# correct layout (document root = public/) Apache never reads this file. If it
# answers a request with 403, the document root points at the wrong place —
# the 403 is the alarm, not the fault. Without it the same mistake serves the
# setup token, password hashes and mail credentials as plain files.
#
# Twin: .releases/htaccess-deny (release layout — deploy.php/switch.php write
# it into the shared/ stores). Keep the functional block identical. Never put
# a deny file into a store served THROUGH public/ (public/media IS
# shared/media — a deny file there denies every image).
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order deny,allow
    Deny from all
</IfModule>
